# Every text file in this distribution is stored, and checked out, with LF endings.
#
# Without this file a clone made on Windows under the default core.autocrlf=true arrives with
# CRLF in the working copy, the POSIX shell scripts under templates/scripts/posix/ included,
# so their shebang line carries a stray CR on a machine that is expected to run them.
#
# The previous release proved the other half of this hazard: CRLF drift inside the shared
# regions was real and simultaneously invisible to the drift checker, because Windows builds
# of gawk open files in text mode and silently discard the CR. That half is fixed with
# BINMODE=3 in lib/posix/check-shared.sh. This file is the half that stops the CRLF from
# arriving at all, which is why both are needed and neither is sufficient alone.
#
# Measured rather than assumed: two identical repositories cloned with core.autocrlf=true, one
# carrying the line below and one not. Without it a shell script arrived as "ASCII text, with
# CRLF line terminators". With it, plain LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images are binary and must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
